{
  "_readme": "THE single file for all manual fixes. Sections: 'lemma' = wrong/missing ECDICT lemma (form -> lemma; same word = treat as its own lemma). 'lexicalizedIng' = -ing words that are nouns in their own right: the main card shows the word's own entry and the verb lemma entry is folded below (running -> run is NOT in this list). 'lexicalizedAdj' = adjectival participles whose adjective sense dominates (tired, scared, boring, complicated…): same treatment (own adjective entry as the main card, verb entry folded below, vocab keyed on the word itself). Gerund -ing words not listed in either list keep resolving to the verb. 'cefr' = manual CEFR level for a word (wins over the CEFR lists; e.g. according -> B1). A whitelist word (lexicalizedIng / lexicalizedAdj) that has no CEFR level of its own automatically uses its verb lemma's level for coverage. 'leadDefs' = a definition placed first on a word's own card, before the ECDICT ones (e.g. the 'according to' sense). 'terms' = names / coined or technical terms missing from ECDICT (key as written; value = short Chinese note). See README 'Per-batch workflow'.",
